--TEST--
`Core\Config::set` of a name with an empty segment returns `false` and adds nothing to `all`, although the `[limits]` row governs its prefix — `rule:config/ini-set-is-core-config-set`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: tools:config/reading-and-changing-it-from-a-program-core-config
// `limits..memory` starts with the `limits` block's name and a dot, so the directive lookup
// finds a row for it. No reader ever asks for that key, so a set of it would change nothing.
uint $before = Core\Arr::count(Core\Config::all());
array<string> $names = ['limits..memory', '.memory', 'memory.', 'limits.memory.'];
foreach ($names as string $name) {
    echo $name, ': ', Core\Config::set($name, '1M') ? 'true' : 'false', "\n";
}
echo Core\Arr::count(Core\Config::all()) == $before ? 'nothing added' : 'added', "\n";
// The dotted spelling without an empty segment is still accepted.
echo 'limits.memory: ', Core\Config::set('limits.memory', '1M') ? 'true' : 'false', "\n";
--EXPECT--
limits..memory: false
.memory: false
memory.: false
limits.memory.: false
nothing added
limits.memory: true
